1. Normally, Carla downloads 2 GB/minute.
textcolor{blue}{First}, calculate the time it takes for Carla to download 200 GB at this rate:
\begin{aligned}
\text{Time} &= \frac{\text{Size}}{\text{Rate}} \qquad \boxed{\text{Time}} &= \frac{200 \text{ GB}}{2 \text{ GB/minute}} \\
\text{Time} &= 100 \text{ minutes or 100/60 = 1 hour and 40 minutes.}
\end{aligned}

2. Next, determine the part of the download that has been completed before Windows forces the restart. Since the download is 200 GB and it took \boxed{1 hour and 40 minutes} to download the whole file, the part already downloaded when the restart happens is:
\begin{aligned}
\text{Already Downloaded} &= \frac{\text{Time Before Restart}}{\text{Total Time}} \times \text{Total Size} \\
\text{Already Downloaded} &= \frac{\text{40 minutes}}{1 \text{ hour and 40 minutes}} \times 200 \text{ GB}
\end{aligned}

In minutes, convert 40 minutes into a fraction of the total minutes:
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\text{40 minutes}}{1 \text{ hour and 40 minutes}} &= \frac{40}{60 + 40} = \frac{40}{100} \\
\text{Already Downloaded} &= \frac{40}{100} \times 200 \text{ GB} \\
\text{Already Downloaded} &= \boxed{80 \text{ GB}}
\end{aligned}

3. Since the restart takes 20 minutes, it will take 1 hour and 40 minutes to download the remaining or the complete file after the restart. From the previous calculations, we know that Carla downloaded 80 GB before the restart:

\begin{aligned}
\text{Size to Download} &= 200 \text{ GB} - 80 \text{ GB} = \boxed{120 \text{ GB}} \\
\text{Time to download the remaining 120 GB} &= \frac{\text{Size}}{\text{Rate}} = \frac{120 \text{ GB}}{2 \text{ GB/minute}} = 60 \text{ minutes or 1 hour}.
\end{aligned}

4. Keep in mind that the restart takes 20 minutes. So, the total time to download the file after the restart is:

\text{Total Downloaded Time} = \boxed{1 \text{ hour and 40 minutes}} (before restart) + \boxed{20 \text{ minutes}} (restart time) + \boxed{1 \text{ hour}} (time to download the remaining file)
Total Downloaded Time = 1 hour and 51 minutes

The final answer is the time it takes to download the entire file after the Windows update restart: \boxed{1 \text{ hour and 51 minutes}}.

